---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import DogGallery from '../components/DogGallery.astro';
import { path } from '../config/paths';
import peter from '../assets/photos/peter.jpg';
import rambo from '../assets/photos/rambo.jpg';
---
<Base
  title="About"
  description="The story of Dogs' Best Friend Rescue Association: who runs it, how it began, and what it does for the street dogs of Ratchaburi, Thailand."
  current="about"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="narrow">
      <p class="eyebrow">About us</p>
      <h1>A small rescue doing difficult work</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Dogs’ Best Friend Rescue Association is a non-profit animal welfare organisation based in Ratchaburi, Thailand.
        We rescue, rehabilitate and rehome stray, unloved and unwanted dogs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-sand">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Where it all began</p>
        <h2>Peter’s story</h2>
        <p>
          Peter first started rescuing dogs in Thailand when he and his wife Khung discovered Beagle puppies being dumped at local
          markets because they did not sell or had health problems. He rescued over 50 of these “dumpster puppies” and found loving homes for them.
        </p>
        <p>
          He then volunteered for over a year as part of a reconstruction crew at a temple shelter, before helping to reduce street dog
          numbers through catch, sterilise and release work.
        </p>
        <p>
          In 2016 Peter started fostering dogs until new families could be found. It isn’t always possible to rehome dogs with difficult
          health or behaviour problems, so the number of dogs at his home grew.
        </p>
        <p>
          To give the dogs more room, and the neighbours some peace, he rented farmland away from the city and started a shelter where the
          dogs could live more freely. That was the start of Dogs’ Best Friend Rescue Association in Ratchaburi.
        </p>
        <blockquote>Peter’s dream is to help those who are suffering live a more comfortable life.</blockquote>
      </div>
      <Image src={peter} alt="Peter and Khung standing on a city street, Khung holding a small black fluffy dog" widths={[400, 720]} sizes="(min-width: 820px) 45vw, 100vw" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="narrow">
      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <ul class="checklist">
        <li><strong>Rescue</strong> sick, injured and unwanted dogs, to end their suffering on the streets.</li>
        <li><strong>Treat</strong> every dog: a wellness check, vet treatment, training and the care they need to recover.</li>
        <li><strong>Foster</strong> dogs in homes for house training and time with people, so each one goes to the right family.</li>
        <li><strong>Sterilise</strong> every dog before rehoming, to help reduce the number of street dogs.</li>
        <li><strong>Rehome</strong> dogs when they’re ready. Adopters go through a strict screening process and training in responsible animal care.</li>
        <li><strong>Give a home for life</strong> at the shelter to dogs who can’t be rehomed because of their health or behaviour.</li>
        <li><strong>Educate</strong>: work with the wider community to teach safe and respectful animal care, so every stray feels safe, respected and loved.</li>
      </ul>
      <h3>Our vision</h3>
      <p>
        To help the local community run mobile sterilisation clinics and wellness checks, so that care is within reach of
        everyone. Please help us work towards an end to the suffering of soi dogs on the streets of Thailand.
      </p>
      <p><a href={path('/get-involved/#partners')}>Meet our partners</a> · <a href={path('/membership/')}>Join the Association</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-sand">
    <div class="wrap split">
      <Image src={rambo} alt="Rambo, a black and tan puppy, walking across the dirt at the shelter" widths={[480, 960]} sizes="(min-width: 820px) 45vw, 100vw" />
      <div>
        <h2>Some go on to new homes</h2>
        <p>
          Rambo was one of the lucky ones. He was rescued, cared for, and adopted by a family in America. Dogs from the rescue have
          travelled to new families abroad with the help of flight volunteers.
        </p>
        <p>Others stay at the shelter for good. Both need the same daily care.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-donate" href={path('/donate/')}>Help keep the rescue running</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Some of the dogs we’ve cared for</h2>
      <DogGallery />
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
